Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:06.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}StyleMorph is a 3D-aware generative model that pulls apart the four things that make an
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.34,0:00:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}image what it is: the object's 3D shape,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.03,0:00:13.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the camera pose, the object's appearance, and the background.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.12,0:00:18.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It does this by learning a 3D morphable model from nothing but ordinary 2D photos,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.62,0:00:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with no 3D scans, no pose labels, and no template supplied by hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.12,0:00:30.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The trick is to morph a single canonical 3D template and render its coordinates into a purely geometric 2D map,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.57,0:00:35.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which then conditions a StyleGAN renderer for photorealistic synthesis.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.34,0:00:37.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On faces, cats, dogs, and wild animals,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.96,0:00:43.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}StyleMorph matches state-of-the-art image quality while giving you independent,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.26,0:00:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}fine-grained control over every factor of variation.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.05,0:00:51.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The dream in 3D-aware image generation is a model you can steer,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.30,0:00:54.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}one where you change the pose without touching identity,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.03,0:00:58.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or swap the background without disturbing the object.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.55,0:01:01.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Today's best 3D-aware GANs make beautiful images,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.81,0:01:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but their hybrid design fuses geometry and appearance together,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.99,0:01:08.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so editing one factor bleeds into the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.98,0:01:13.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Classical 3D morphable models solve the control problem elegantly,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.37,0:01:18.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet they require expensive 3D scanning and painstaking manual alignment,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.16,0:01:21.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which is why they mainly exist for human faces.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.28,0:01:27.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}StyleMorph asks whether we can get morphable-model control for arbitrary object categories,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.33,0:01:30.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}learning everything from unstructured 2D images alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.22,0:01:37.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Morphable models are the workhorse of visual effects and augmented reality because they hand creators clean,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.06,0:01:41.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}separate dials for pose, expression, and appearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.36,0:01:48.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The question that motivates this work is simple: can we get that same level of control inside a modern 3D-aware GAN,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.71,0:01:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but without any of the 3D supervision that morphable models normally need?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.40,0:01:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Prior work that added 3D deformations to synthesis either stayed limited to a single dynamic scene,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.67,0:02:04.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or leaned on a deformable template that already existed for the category.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.30,0:02:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}StyleMorph instead turns the morphable model itself into something the network discovers from unlabeled 2D images,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.52,0:02:14.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}making it a first-class citizen of generative modelling.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.37,0:02:19.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}StyleMorph makes three linked contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.19,0:02:22.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.01,0:02:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it learns a 3D morphable model of an object category's non-rigid shape variation using nothing but 2D images,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.83,0:02:30.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}by morphing a canonical template through backpropagation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.66,0:02:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second, it introduces Template Object Coordinates,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.48,0:02:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}or TOCS: a deformable cousin of Normalized Object Coordinates that gives every surface
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.30,0:02:42.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}point a stable template identity and acts as a powerful,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.12,0:02:45.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}deformation-equivariant descriptor of shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.94,0:02:49.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.76,0:02:53.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it feeds 2D TOCS maps as a purely geometric conditioning signal into a StyleGAN-based deferred neural renderer,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.59,0:02:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}cleanly separating shape from appearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.41,0:03:01.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Together these deliver disentangled control over pose, shape, object appearance,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.23,0:03:04.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and background, all at high resolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.35,0:03:06.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The method has two halves.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.05,0:03:08.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the geometry side,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.42,0:03:14.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a Morphable Renderer learns a deformation-free object in canonical template coordinates
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.12,0:03:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}as a constant implicit function.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.21,0:03:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A SIREN-based deformation field, driven by a shape code,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.87,0:03:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}warps each camera ray from world space into that template space by adding a predicted offset.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.95,0:03:31.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Integrating the template coordinates along each ray produces a 2D map called a TOCS map,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.71,0:03:36.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which encodes the compounded effects of shape deformation, camera pose,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.36,0:03:39.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and perspective, and nothing about appearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.36,0:03:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the synthesis side,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.80,0:03:46.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a StyleGAN2-based deferred neural renderer takes this geometric TOCS map together with
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.43,0:03:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}two independent appearance codes,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.59,0:03:52.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}one for the foreground object and one for the background scene,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.71,0:03:55.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and generates a high-resolution image.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.19,0:04:00.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The foreground and background are composited with an alpha mask predicted by the model.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.88,0:04:06.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Training proceeds in two stages: first the deformable volume renderer learns realistic
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.51,0:04:10.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}shape at low resolution with weak silhouette supervision,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.24,0:04:15.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}then it is frozen and used only to supply TOCS maps while the 2D renderer is trained for
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.99,0:04:18.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}photorealistic full-resolution output.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.78,0:04:22.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}StyleMorph is evaluated on four widely used image datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.86,0:04:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FFHQ contributes seventy thousand centered human face photos with a range of challenging backgrounds and poses.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.53,0:04:36.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The AFHQ collection adds animal faces in three splits: roughly fifty-six hundred cats,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.48,0:04:40.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}fifty-two hundred dogs, and fifty-two hundred wild animals.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.56,0:04:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The authors report Frechet Inception Distance at two-fifty-six resolution,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.68,0:04:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}comparing against eleven state-of-the-art 3D-aware GAN baselines,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.17,0:04:56.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}so the results test both photorealism on faces and the ability to generalize to animal
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.12,0:04:59.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}categories that classical morphable models never covered.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.36,0:05:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The headline finding is that disentanglement does not have to cost image quality.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.71,0:05:11.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}StyleMorph reaches a Frechet Inception Distance of seven point nine one on FFHQ faces,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.39,0:05:16.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and four point two nine on cats, three point four nine on wild animals,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.09,0:05:20.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and thirteen point nine five on dogs, all at two-fifty-six resolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.71,0:05:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}These numbers sit right alongside the strongest 3D-aware GANs that offer none of StyleMorph's control.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.45,0:05:31.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The comparison that matters most is against Disentangled3D,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.35,0:05:37.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the only prior method that also represents shape with a deformable template: StyleMorph's
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.23,0:05:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FFHQ score of seven point nine one is far ahead of its twenty-eight point one eight,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.78,0:05:47.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and StyleMorph additionally separates foreground from background,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.08,0:05:48.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which that method does not.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.16,0:05:52.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The ablations, all run under a fair ninety-six-hour training budget,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.97,0:05:56.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}isolate each design choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.77,0:06:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Swapping TOCS for plain NOCS raises FID from about eight point three to eight point nine
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.58,0:06:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and blurs the conditioning signal,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.39,0:06:08.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}showing template-space coordinates matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.20,0:06:11.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Removing the deformable module and using a direct occupancy network instead keeps FID
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.00,0:06:15.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}similar but drastically worsens the consistency scores,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.81,0:06:19.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}proving the value of modelling shape through deformation.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.62,0:06:23.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Switching from late fusion to early fusion nudges FID down slightly but badly hurts alpha consistency,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.42,0:06:27.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}letting foreground and background bleed together.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.23,0:06:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Finally,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.04,0:06:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}directly optimizing view consistency as a differentiable loss does improve that metric,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.85,0:06:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}from nearly sixteen down to eight, but it trades away image quality,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.65,0:06:42.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}pushing FID up to twelve point three.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.76,0:06:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers capture the impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.09,0:06:49.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On FFHQ faces StyleMorph scores a seven point nine one FID,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.25,0:06:54.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}versus twenty-eight point one eight for the only competing template-based method.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.96,0:07:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On animals it reaches four point two nine on cats, three point four nine on wild,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.67,0:07:03.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and thirteen point nine five on dogs.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.28,0:07:09.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It disentangles four independent factors: shape, camera pose, foreground appearance,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.20,0:07:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and background appearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.04,0:07:17.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And the core TOCS-versus-NOCS ablation shows template coordinates improving FID from eight
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.38,0:07:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}point nine to eight point three while also sharpening disentanglement.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.32,0:07:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}All of this is learned from unstructured 2D images, with no 3D supervision at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.40,0:07:36.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The one-line takeaway is that StyleMorph delivers morphable-model control inside a state-of-the-art image generator,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.18,0:07:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}learned entirely from ordinary 2D photos.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.93,0:07:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}By morphing a learned canonical template and rendering it into a purely geometric TOCS map,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.03,0:07:49.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it hands a StyleGAN renderer a clean geometric signal, so shape, pose,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.73,0:07:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}object appearance,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.93,0:07:56.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and background can each be edited independently without sacrificing photorealism.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.37,0:08:01.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In effect it builds an unsupervised 3D morphable model for general object categories,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.07,0:08:08.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}extending the fine-grained controllability that visual-effects artists rely on from faces to cats,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.64,0:08:10.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}dogs, and wild animals.
